WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:06.490
Kaina City, Hoenn Region

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:05.650
After receiving an urgent summons
from Project Mew,

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:08.660
Go has arrived at Kaina City
in the Hoenn Region.

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:13.410
Um... The lab is...

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:14.620
Go!

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.910
Tokio!

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:22.710
The search for Mew
is finally here!

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:23.500
Yeah!

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.880
And we even
get to participate together!

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:29.130
I was so excited,
I couldn’t sleep last night.

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:31.140
That’s no good.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.640
You ought to make sure
you’re in peak condition.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.140
Shigeru!

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.140
Shigeru, friend!

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.930
What a pity, Go.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:38.850
Huh?

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:42.810
Satoshi’s Masters Tournament
finals match is today, right?

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:44.150
Yeah.

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:46.780
But I just know he’ll win.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.320
We promised one another...

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.780
...that next time we meet,
we’ll meet with a smile!

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:57.910
Interesting.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:00:59.000
Yeah.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.370
Hey, we should hurry.

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:02.210
Professor Hodaka will be waiting.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:19.810
Satoshi...
Give it all you’ve got.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.070
Give it all you’ve got...

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:28.690
...Go.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:33.820
Shoot Stadium, Galar Region

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:15.630
The Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament.

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:17.930
Today, at last, we have the finals!

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:22.010
In this event, we saw a lineup
of Champions from various regions,

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:25.690
the rarely-matched spectacle
of an all-star Masters Eight!

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:29.860
The two who took down this lineup
of powerhouses to become finalists...

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:33.440
...are moments away from clashing
on the battlefield!

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:37.450
One will be the trainer standing
at the summit of Pokémon battling!

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:44.200
Everyone!

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:46.870
You ready to go?!

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:57.260
We’re gonna win!

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:03.560
Wha—?

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:04.520
Satoshi!

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:05.980
Excuse us!

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:07.100
Huh?!

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.480
Hikari! And Koharu!

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.060
We came here to cheer for you.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:14.280
I’ll be cheering extra,
to make up for Go.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:16.070
You will? Thanks!

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:17.360
Plus...

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:21.370
I wanted to show her
an official match, too.

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:26.870
I’ve been watching everything on TV too,
but I just couldn’t sit back and watch from afar!

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:29.120
The whole Institute’s
cheering for you, too.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:31.330
Do your best, Satoshi!

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:32.380
Yeah!

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:36.840
Big Bro...

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.720
This is a nice sense of tension...

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:48.060
I wonder why...

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:51.770
...I’m reminded of
the first day I ever battled.

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:06.330
Now, the two Pokémon Trainers seeking to
stand upon the summit are finally arriving.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.170
Pochama’s so cute!

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:14.540
Great, huh?

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:17.380
This is how we cheered him on
back in Sinnoh!

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:21.260
Would Eevee like to try it?

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:21.840
Huh?

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:29.980
That’s so cute!

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:33.190
You look great, Eevee!

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:36.400
Who’d have thought
the brat boy would make it this far?

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.780
Let’s take it up a notch
with live-streamed commentary!

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:40.820
Don’t forget our goal, meow!

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:41.650
Huh?

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:46.240
Today, we’ll finally find out who has
the strongest Pokémon, fit for Team Rocket, meow!

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:48.740
I forgot about that!

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:52.500
We can’t complete our mission
if we don’t catch them!

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:54.170
Let’s keep a diligent watch!

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:56.630
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:06.600
Now then,
the finalists are here.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:13.440
Ranked 8th in the Masters Eight,
the first Champion of Alola...

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:17.650
Hailing from Kanto,
Competitor Satoshi.

00:06:17.650 --> 00:06:19.230
Go for it!

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:20.190
Give it your all!

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:21.030
Satoshi!

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:23.780
I’m cheering for you!

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:30.410
Go for it, go for it, Satoshi!
Go for it, go for it, Satoshi!

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:30.410
Everyone’s cheering for Satoshi...

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:36.250
This is no time to be streaming!

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:37.960
You said it! Call it off!

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:40.920
We have to cheer
for the brat boy, meow!

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:47.470
Ever since entering the Championships,
he’s defeated strong opponents one after another.

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:50.430
The tournament’s
most promising trainer.

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:55.940
During the tournament, he’s defeated
Competitor Daigo, the Champion of Hoenn...

00:06:55.940 --> 00:07:01.190
...and even emerged victorious against
Competitor Shirona, the Champion of Sinnoh.

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:09.910
Wielding Daimax, Z-Moves and Mega Evolution,
he uses unique ideas in his Pokémon battles.

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:12.700
So, what inspired plays
does he have for us today?

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:16.710
And facing Competitor Satoshi...

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:19.840
...is the unrivaled Monarch
that everyone knows.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:25.800
The object of admiration and goal
of Pokémon Trainers around the world!

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:28.640
Ranked 1st in the Masters Eight!

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:32.680
The Champion of Galar,
Competitor Dande!

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:36.310
Big bro!

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:37.560
Hop.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:39.980
Sonia! You made it!

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:42.610
Thought I had to
watch this up close.

00:07:42.610 --> 00:07:47.610
Now, will Competitor Satoshi be able to
put an end to his undefeated win streak?

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:52.870
Or will Competitor Dande’s
win streak only be extended?

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:56.160
A truly climactic match!

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:01.420
Satoshi! So we finally meet
upon the battlefield!

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:03.840
Yeah! And...

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:04.920
...in the finals!

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:10.930
There’s no better stage!
No one has been looking forward to our battle more...

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:13.760
...than <i>me!</i>

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:24.690
Competing on equal footing with Champions...
He truly has grown remarkably!

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:29.030
Yup! Trust your Pokémon
and try your best, Satoshi!

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:32.910
The finals are a 6v6 full battle!

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:37.790
There is no limit on match length
or switching out Pokémon.

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:42.670
Whoever makes all six of their opponent’s Pokémon
unable to battle will be the winner.

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:48.510
Additionally, you are allowed a single use of only one
of the following: Daimax, a Z-Move, or Mega Evolu—

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:49.550
Hold it!

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:53.350
Competitor Dande...

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:57.810
“Only one” is no fun!
Use all of them, Satoshi!

00:08:58.850 --> 00:08:59.810
All of them?

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:03.860
This is a serious match,
the climactic match!

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:07.070
I and my Pokémon will be facing you
with everything we have.

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:11.570
So I want you and your Pokémon
to face me with everything you have, too!

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:14.910
Daimax, Z-Moves, Mega Evolution...

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:17.080
I wanna fight them all!

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:20.830
And then beat them all!
Everyone, what do you think?

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:23.790
Don’t you want to see him
battle at full-power?!

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:28.960
Yeah! That’s my bro!
What a great idea!

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:31.590
Woohoo! Yay!

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:31.590
What does that mean?

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:33.890
It means this is gonna be incredible!

00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:36.060
Go get him, Satoshi!

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:41.020
Yes... Yes... Understood.

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:48.320
The Championships Management
has accepted Competitor Dande’s suggestion.

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:50.490
Competitor Satoshi, do you accept?

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:52.950
Of course! I’ll do it!

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:55.570
Unprecedented!

00:09:55.570 --> 00:10:02.210
Competitor Dande’s suggestion will turn this finals match
into a never-before-seen, full-spec, super battle!

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:05.210
That’s just like Competitor Dande.

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:06.210
Yes.

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:09.510
This will be a heated battle
like none before.

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:14.260
Now then, both battlers,
send your first Pokémon out onto the field!

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:15.220
Three!

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:16.180
Two!

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:17.140
One!

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:18.140
Go!

00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:20.640
Pikachu, I choose you!

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:24.770
Come out, Aceburn!

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:38.580
I’m counting on you, Pikachu!
I decided you’d go first!

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:44.710
No thought to tactics, then.

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:48.040
Let’s crush him, Aceburn!

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:53.340
Big Bro’s Aceburn
is the strongest striker.

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:56.090
Let the battle begin!

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:57.510
100,000 Volts!

00:11:00.140 --> 00:11:01.560
Scorching Sands!

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:21.700
Aceburn and Pikachu’s attacks...

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:24.540
...both hit simultaneously!

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:31.340
Whoa! Aceburn was completely unfazed
by the 100,000 Volts!

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:33.050
What?!

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:49.270
Let the battle begin!

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:50.690
100,000 Volts!

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:54.740
Scorching Sands!

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:14.880
Aceburn and Pikachu’s attacks...

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:17.720
...both hit simultaneously!

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:21.010
What?!

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:25.390
The Ground-type Scorching Sands
was super effective on Pikachu!

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:29.400
On the other hand, a direct hit
from 100,000 Volts left Aceburn unharmed.

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:31.900
Could this mean...?

00:12:34.820 --> 00:12:37.400
Satoshi... first time
seeing the Ability Libero?

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:39.150
Libero...

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:43.620
When this guy uses an attack,
it becomes the type of the move.

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:46.830
Does that mean Aceburn’s...
a Ground type right now?

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:51.000
Pikachu, return!

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:54.840
If electricity won’t work...

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:56.920
...then that’s his only option.

00:12:58.670 --> 00:12:59.800
You okay?

00:13:00.930 --> 00:13:02.760
Come watch the others battle.

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:06.140
Return, Aceburn!

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:10.890
Come out, Inteleon!

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:13.360
Gänger, I choose you!

00:13:19.990 --> 00:13:21.910
Now an Inteleon...

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:24.660
It’s like I’m battling Go’s Pokémon.

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:26.910
Let’s do it! Snipe Shot!

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:28.040
Shadow Ball!

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:37.250
Hit it!

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:42.130
Evil Pulse!

00:13:45.180 --> 00:13:46.430
Gänger, dodge it!

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:49.770
That won’t work.

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:51.020
Aqua Jet!

00:13:58.980 --> 00:13:59.900
What’s that?

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:03.530
Counter Shield...

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:11.540
It’s the spinning tactic Competitor Satoshi
and Pikachu used in the semifinals, replicated perfectly!

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:16.790
Satoshi! I added that interesting trick
of yours to my arsenal.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:20.420
I’m impressed, Mr. Dande.

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:32.180
Gänger!

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:38.820
Quite a surprise, wasn’t it?

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:43.240
That means hiding’s pointless...

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:47.370
Satoshi’s under some real pressure.

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:48.280
Yes.

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:53.540
Competitor Dande’s greed... Even mastering
his rival’s techniques if it helps him win...

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:57.670
And Inteleon marvelously pulls it off!

00:14:57.670 --> 00:14:59.670
Gänger! Use Will-O-Wisp!

00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:10.890
Watch out, Inteleon!

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:16.770
Return, Gänger!

00:15:21.570 --> 00:15:23.440
Let’s get huge!

00:15:25.030 --> 00:15:25.650
Here it is.

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:29.070
Kyodaimax!

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:50.680
Competitor Satoshi
decides to activate Kyodaimax!

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:54.140
How will Competitor Dande
respond to this?!

00:15:57.940 --> 00:15:59.190
Snipe Shot!

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:04.940
What? With both hands?

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:07.990
Big Bro’s Inteleon can dual wield!

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:10.450
Kyodai Phantom!

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:31.220
They both took damage!

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:33.430
All right!

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:35.100
You really went and did it.

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:40.230
Due to the effect of Kyodai Phantom,
Competitor Dande can’t switch Pokémon!

00:16:40.230 --> 00:16:43.730
Big Bro can still do this,
even if he can’t switch!

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:44.940
Evil Pulse!

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:48.990
Dai Acid!

00:17:00.420 --> 00:17:02.290
Gänger! Full power!

00:17:10.430 --> 00:17:12.470
Fire!

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:26.070
Inteleon!

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:36.580
Dai Acid lands a direct hit
on Inteleon!

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:42.540
And perhaps the Evil Pulse hit a critical point,
because Gänger has returned to normal size.

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:46.460
Inteleon is unable to battle!

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:52.720
The first win of the finals
goes to Competitor Satoshi!

00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:54.930
All right!

00:17:56.600 --> 00:17:58.850
This can’t be real...
Big Bro...

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:05.730
He did it!

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:11.570
Begin with your first win...

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:13.570
Gäge-chan did well, too.

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:15.160
Good going, oh!

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:16.200
Ohh!

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:18.160
Gänger, good work, meow!

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:22.660
See that, “strongest guy”?!
That’s what the brat boy can do, oh!

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:32.300
You okay, Gänger?

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:36.140
Return, Inteleon!

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:41.270
You fought well.

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:43.020
I’ll build upon that base.

00:18:44.270 --> 00:18:46.770
I’ll catch up to you, Satoshi!

00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:51.650
He’s ignited.

00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:55.410
He’s amazing
when he gets like that.

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:58.280
Come out, Barrikohru!

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:04.410
Competitor Dande’s third Pokémon
is Barrikohru!

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:07.000
Sludge Bomb!

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:08.460
Freeze-Dry!

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:19.720
The Sludge Bombs were frozen!

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:30.020
Barikohru! Freeze-Dry!

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:39.030
It looks like Barrikohru
can’t manage to attack.

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:41.370
The ability Cursed Body, huh?

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:44.580
Yeah! You won’t be using
Freeze-Dry for a while!

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:46.160
You think that can stop me?

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:54.920
Gänger is frozen!
The fearsome power of Freeze-Dry!

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:56.760
No way...

00:19:58.140 --> 00:19:59.300
Psycho Field!

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:10.270
A Psycho Field unfolds!
That’ll increase the strength of Psychic-type moves!

00:20:11.570 --> 00:20:12.940
What do you think?

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:16.320
Now the battlefield
has become a stage for Barrikohru.

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:19.450
Wide Force!

00:20:32.170 --> 00:20:33.000
Gänger!

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:39.010
Gänger is unable to battle!

00:20:40.430 --> 00:20:43.640
With the effect of Psycho Field
and the powered-up Wide Force,

00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:48.390
this time Competitor Dande takes a win!
In an instant, he’s evened the score!

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:50.400
All right!

00:20:55.070 --> 00:20:57.530
He was done in, meow...

00:20:58.070 --> 00:20:59.530
Return, Gänger!

00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:03.830
You fought well.

00:21:07.040 --> 00:21:10.540
I dedicate this victory to Inteleon.

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:13.790
His hard work is what enabled it.

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:18.840
As I suppose you know,
what you do in a full battle...

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:21.800
...is use your Pokémon
to build up damage on the opponent,

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:24.800
seizing each victory as a team.

00:21:29.230 --> 00:21:34.110
The Masters Tournament finals
see a fierce battle unfold from the outset.

00:21:34.110 --> 00:21:37.440
Dande and Satoshi
each claim one victory,

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:41.320
as an even more fervent, fierce fight shakes
the battlefield.

00:23:06.410 --> 00:23:10.870
Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament News!

00:23:11.910 --> 00:23:14.460
The finals battle between Competitor Satoshi
and Competitor Dande!

00:23:14.460 --> 00:23:17.290
Currently,
they’ve each lost one Pokémon!

00:23:17.290 --> 00:23:18.790
The battle is even, meow!

00:23:18.790 --> 00:23:21.710
And that... Barribarrikohru, was it?
That sure gets on my nerves.

00:23:21.710 --> 00:23:22.800
It’s “Barrikohru”!

00:23:22.800 --> 00:23:24.170
And come on, we’re live!

00:23:24.170 --> 00:23:26.300
Look forward to
the next battle, meow!

